        <p class="faq-a">There is no universal answer — it depends on how fast property prices are growing in your target market, your income stability, and your risk tolerance. In high-growth markets like Sydney, buying sooner with a smaller deposit often results in greater long-term wealth, because price growth outpaces LMI costs. In stable or slower-growing markets, the case for saving a larger deposit is stronger. Compare the numbers for your specific situation using <a href="/australia/mortgage-calculator/">CalcPhi's Mortgage Calculator</a> and <a href="/australia/rent-vs-buy-calculator/">Rent vs Buy Calculator</a>.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>


